cessing-and-machine-learning-spring-2018/d6b9603509fe7de36c57a0ed8ebd92d2_chart_300.jpg\" srcset=\"/courses/18-065-matrix-methods-in-data-analysis-signal-processing-and-machine-learning-spring-2018/d6b9603509fe7de36c57a0ed8ebd92d2_chart_300.jpg?format=auto&amp;quality=75&amp;width=480 480w, /courses/18-065-matrix-methods-in-data-analysis-signal-processing-and-machine-learning-spring-2018/d6b9603509fe7de36c57a0ed8ebd92d2_chart_300.jpg?format=auto&amp;quality=75&amp;width=800 800w, /courses/18-065-matrix-methods-in-data-analysis-signal-processing-and-machine-learning-spring-2018/d6b9603509fe7de36c57a0ed8ebd92d2_chart_300.jpg?format=auto&amp;quality=75&amp;width=1280 1280w, /courses/18-065-matrix-methods-in-data-analysis-signal-processing-and-machine-learning-spring-2018/d6b9603509fe7de36c57a0ed8ebd92d2_chart_300.jpg?format=auto&amp;quality=75&amp;width=1920 1920w\"/>\n<h3 id=\"textbook\">Textbook</h3>\n<p>Strang, Gilbert.Â <em>Linear Algebra and Learning from Data</em>.Â <a aria-label=\"Wellesley-Cambridge Press (opens in a new tab)\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.wellesleycambridge.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Wellesley-Cambridge Press</a>, 2019. ISBN: 9780692196380.</p>\n<p>Professor Strang created <a aria-label=\"a website for the book (opens in a new tab)\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://math.mit.edu/~gs/learningfromdata/\" target=\"_blank\">a website for the book</a>, including a link to the <a aria-label=\"Table of Contents (PDF) (opens in a new tab)\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://math.mit.edu/~gs/learningfromdata/dsla_toc.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Table of Contents (PDF)</a>, sample chapters, and essays on <a aria-label=\"Deep Learning (PDF) (opens in a new tab)\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://math.mit.edu/%7Egs/learningfromdata/SIAM03.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Learning (PDF)</a> and <a aria-label=\"Neural Nets (PDF) (opens in a new tab)\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://math.mit.edu/%7Egs/learningfromdata/dsla_dlnn.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Neural Nets (PDF)</a>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"requirements-and-grading\">Requirements and Grading</h3>\n<p>There are homework assignments, labs, and a final project. The grade is based on all three elements. NOTE to OCW USERS: The OCW site includes problems assigned for every lecture, aligned with readings in the course textbook. The on-campus students had weekly problem sets.</p>\n</main>",
